Typical Instruments: Massive, multi-oscillator modular synthesizers (especially those capable of complex, evolving arpeggios and 432Hz tone generation), clean electric guitars with extensive use of delay and chorus, traditional drum kits often augmented with electronic percussion layers, male and female operatic lead vocals (often in unison or harmony), and highly processed, layered whistles.

